Chapter: RocRecJsonList
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_recursive_data_tests.zig, the
 four "recursive nominal json" cases, which build

     Json := [Null, Bool(Bool), Number(I64), Array(List(Json))]

 and inspect `Null`, `Bool(True)`, `Number(42)` and `Array([])`. The port
 prints all four through a hand-written printer, then one value the cases do
 not build, `Array([Number(1), Null, Array([])])`, because a recursive sum
 reached only through a List is the shape worth the port.

Section: Types

  Json =
   | Null
   | Bool (Boolean)
   | Number (Integer)
   | Array (List Json)

Section: Functions

  json-text : Json -> Text
  json-text (j) =
   when j
    is Null -> "Null"
    is Bool (b) -> if b then "Bool(True)" else "Bool(False)"
    is Number (n) -> "Number(" & show n & ")"
    is Array (items) -> "Array([" & join-json items 0 & "])"

  join-json : List Json, Integer -> Text
  join-json (items) (i) =
   if i >= list-length items then ""
   else if i + 1 == list-length items then json-text (list-at items i)
   else json-text (list-at items i) & ", " & join-json items (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (json-text Null)
   print-line-uni (json-text (Bool True))
   print-line-uni (json-text (Number 42))
   print-line-uni (json-text (Array []))
   print-line-uni (json-text (Array [Number 1, Null, Array []]))
  end
